## Scientific And Domain Assessments

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/1-naphtylacetic_Acid.yaml.

Compared 1-Naphthylacetic acid (CHEBI:32918) to 1 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

mediadive.ingredient:2436: The source names Duchefa N0903. Duchefa identifies 1-naphthaleneacetic acid CAS 86-87-3, consistent with CHEBI:32918 and the current owner; the Naphtylacetic spelling is a supported source variant. Remaining requirement: Retain existing native review and token holds until the full exported payload is reconciled.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/2-mercaptoethanesulfonate.yaml.

Compared 2-Mercaptoethanesulfonate (CHEBI:17905) to 1 assigned source cases. Bounded isolated owner changes proposed: B-PROPOSAL-2-mercaptoethanesulfonate. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Mercaptoethanesulfonic acid: M2642 explicitly describes mercaptoethanesulfonic acid as coenzyme M in a 100X stock, while M3253 names the acid as a component. ChEBI17905 denotes the acid; sodium mesna and deprotonated coenzyme M are separate. The source occurrences denote the solute, not the entire 100X preparation. Remaining requirement: None

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Bovine_Serum_Albumin.yaml.

Compared bovine serum albumin (NCIT:C85253) to 2 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Albumin Fraction V Bovine (Sigma A9647): Sigma A9647 is bovine serum albumin, currently described as heat-shock fraction, pH7, lyophilized powder; the three recipes call it fractionV in OADC stock. The maintained Bovine_Serum_Albumin record already preserves A9647 as a source-specific supplied form and explicitly forbids making fraction/product names exact generic synonyms. Preserve that prior ruling. Remaining requirement: None

Albumin fraction V, bovine: The ten occurrences specify bovine albumin fraction V, often inside OADC enrichment. Fraction V is preparation information and does not prove all suppliers, catalog formulations or the full OADC mixture are identical to generic bovine serum albumin. Existing generic-owner ruling preserves supplier/form detail separately. Remaining requirement: Identify the fraction-V product in each original source before adding supplied_form; retain OADC nesting and do not add a universal resolving fraction-V synonym.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Ca-folinate.yaml.

Compared Ca-folinate (CHEBI:31340) to 1 assigned source cases. Bounded isolated owner changes proposed: B-PROPOSAL-Ca-folinate. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Calcium folinic acid: M539 explicitly adds calcium folinic acid in its cofactor solution. CHEBI31340 is calcium folinate; the free folinic acid CHEBI15640 lacks the calcium counterion. This supports the existing salt identity without assigning a specific 6S/6R product or hydrate. Remaining requirement: None

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: concern. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Calcium_Pantothenate.yaml.

Compared Calcium pantothenate (CHEBI:31345) to 3 assigned source cases. Bounded isolated owner changes proposed: W07-COMBINED-Calcium_Pantothenate. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Ca-panthothenate: CCAP UCM explicitly writes Ca-panthothenate in its vitamin stock but supplies no stereochemistry. The maintained calcium pantothenate structure is D-specific and contains conflicting DL aliases; typo normalization does not choose D over DL. Remaining requirement: Obtain the UCM vitamin stock product/CAS or stereochemical specification; distinguish calcium D-pantothenate from the racemate before adding an exact alias.

Calcium D(+)-panthothenate: M1666/M1667 explicitly retain D(+) in Calcium D(+)-panthothenate. The extra h is a spelling variant of the D-pantothenate calcium salt; the D label supports the maintained D-specific structure but does not rescue its unrelated or DL aliases. Remaining requirement: None

mediadive.ingredient:878: Source CAS 137-08-6 identifies calcium D-pantothenate, CHEBI:31345. Four vanillylamide/Zostrix aliases on its current owner instead occur on CHEBI:3374 capsaicin, a chemically different substance; they are demonstrably foreign identity labels. Remaining requirement: Coordinator must compose this baseline-relative proposal with the separately reviewed B-part alias proposal and retain other owner review findings; issue 1157 already tracks this contamination.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: unknown. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Cellostatin.yaml.

Compared Cellostatin (kgmicrobe.compound:cellostatin) to 1 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

kgmicrobe.compound:cellostatin: The original cellostatin publication documents an antibiotic isolated from a Streptomyces strain. That supports a named natural-product entity but the captured publication/index does not establish a verified chemical structure, CAS or exact ontology identity. The exact OLS name search returned no term. Remaining requirement: A primary structural characterization or authoritative registry record linking cellostatin to a specific structure and supplied form is required for promotion; discovery/production evidence alone is insufficient.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: unknown. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Citric_Acid.yaml.

Compared Citric acid (CHEBI:30769) to 1 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

mediadive.ingredient:1997: JCM 1105 explicitly uses trisodium citrate trihydrate, while MediaDive cross-references CAS 6132-05-4 and formula C6H8O7.3/2H2O.2Na, inconsistent with the stated trisodium trihydrate. The rejected association with free citric acid does not repair the hydrate conflict. Remaining requirement: Obtain a reagent certificate or corrected primary recipe identifying whether the three-water material is intended and its exact registry identity.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Cyanocobalamin.yaml.

Compared Cyanocobalamin (CHEBI:17439) to 5 assigned source cases. Bounded isolated owner changes proposed: W07-COMBINED-Cyanocobalamin. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12): Both source occurrences explicitly say Cyanocobalamin, with VitaminB12 as a parenthetical gloss. CCAP stock4 and NBRC1550 support this named vitamer; the frozen CHEBI176843 class on one occurrence is broader than the explicit compound. CHEBI17439 is the matching cyanocobalamin identity. Add only this fully qualified alias, not generic VitaminB12. Remaining requirement: None

Cyanocobalamine (vitamin B12): DSMZ958 and Togo M2300 explicitly name cyanocobalamine with vitamin B12 parenthetical. The cyano-qualified substance is CHEBI17439; the broader vitamin-B12 class CHEBI176843 does not replace that specificity. Remaining requirement: None

Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin): The complete frozen UTEX DAS cocktail occurrence explicitly names Sigma V6629 in its ingredient evidence. The original UTEX recipe repeats that catalog, and the official supplier identifies V6629 as cyanocobalamin, CAS68-19-9. Therefore this occurrence supports cyanocobalamin rather than merely the unspecified vitaminB12 class. The product specification, not the5.9µM quantity or generic word cobalamin, establishes the vitamer. Remaining requirement: Apply only the source-bound UTEX DAS occurrence correction to CHEBI:17439; no global Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin) alias is proposed. Preserve the original label and source sterilization instructions.

Cyanocobalamin (B12): The P5 RS NM component explicitly names Cyanocobalamin (B12), so its frozen vitamin-B12 class pointer is broader than the stated vitamer. The nested stock rate 1 g/L describes the cyanocobalamin solute, not the identity or full carrier formulation of the stock. Remaining requirement: None

mediadive.ingredient:847: CAS 68-19-9 and the source chemical fields identify cyanocobalamin, CHEBI:17439. CHEBI:176843 vitamin B12 denotes the broader vitamin class and does not authorize moving this precise chemical into a generic-vitamer identity. Remaining requirement: Reconcile the competing vitamin-class alias and inherited owner-payload holds before source consumption.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: supported. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/DNA_From_Salmon.yaml.

Compared DNA from Salmon (cas:438545-06-3) to 1 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

Salmon sperm DNA (Sigma): TOGO M2215 explicitly specifies salmon sperm DNA from Sigma. This preserves organism/tissue and supplier scope; neither generic DNA nor the herring-sperm alias in Fish-sperm_Dna establishes equivalent material. The maintained DNA_From_Salmon CAS record also lacks proof it denotes this exact sperm-derived supplier product. Remaining requirement: Recover the Sigma catalogue identifier or original material specification before equating this preparation with an existing salmon DNA owner; retain tissue origin and supplier meanwhile.

### Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison

identity: unknown. Targets: data/ingredients/mapped/Disodium_Malate.yaml.

Compared Disodium Malate (CHEBI:91260) to 1 assigned source cases. No owner-byte change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation or contrast; no complete owner approval.

DL--sodium Malate: JCM566’s direct page is unavailable, while the frozen TOGO M570 component explicitly retains DL sodium malate. This racemate cannot be an exact alias on Sodium_Malate CHEBI91261 (S-specific). CHEBI91260 disodium malate is a comparison candidate but the source still lacks sodium stoichiometry. Remaining requirement: Recover the M570/JCM566 supplied salt stoichiometry/hydration; preserve DL and do not infer disodium or L identity from existing mixed owner synonyms.

