mediadive.ingredient:1621: Whole egg is a biological material. The source gives 200 mL but no species or preparation specification; it cannot be represented by a single chemical, isolated yolk, or a species-specific egg identity from name alone. Remaining requirement: An originating recipe or supplier specification naming species, processing and whether the intact edible contents are meant is required for a more specific material owner.

## Findings

### F1: Scutellarin aliases resolve a chemically different sodium dithionite owner

blocker / open / confirmed; issue key: dithionite-foreign-scutellarin-aliases.

Six active scutellarin-derived aliases contradict CHEBI:61278 versus CHEBI:66870. The isolated proposal rejects the six strings while preserving their provenance and adds only the independently supported source alias.

### F2: Racemic sodium lactate alias resolves an L-specific owner

blocker / open / confirmed; issue key: l-lactate-dl-synonym-conflict.

The active Sodium D,L-Lactate synonym conflicts with this L-specific CHEBI:232798 owner. The proposed rejection and explicit L source spelling do not authorize racemic or unknown-stereo source cases.

### F3: Capsaicin names contaminate the calcium pantothenate owner

blocker / open / confirmed; issue key: calcium-pantothenate-capsaicin-aliases.

Four vanillylamide, capsaicin and Zostrix strings belong to CHEBI:3374, not CHEBI:31345. Their rejection does not settle all D versus DL source cases or inherited supplier assertions.

### F4: QSY9 dye and preparation instruction are resolving stock synonyms

blocker / open / confirmed; issue key: cysteine-stock-qsy9-alias.

CHEBI:52891 denotes QSY9 succinimidyl ester, a different substance. Reject the dye string and preparation instruction while keeping the solution separate from pure cysteine hydrochloride and retaining unresolved concentration/form relations.

