| case-165 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[165] case_id=KG_CASE:67304cd492c605f3f189b52bb0876d1f6865412fbedf46e40020e9a287e44417 | partial | Sigma 155322 establishes trans-styrylacetic acid CAS 1914-58-5 and trans structure; exact-name and CAS OLS searches found no hit in their scopes. The current registry denotes that named substance, but a compliant CAS promotion still needs a verified nearest ontology parent. Scope: This is the independent metatraits_gtdb source case, with blank raw label retained. Matching the normalized name does not prove reagent form or recover the original trait-assay context. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-166 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[166] case_id=KG_CASE:67b7093aa01e7ccfcbc31bef2eb616170caac68564688ec849b8d1266566448c | partial | OLS lists L-alanine-4-nitroanilide among mesh:C004813 synonyms, but native NLM makes L concept M0045996 explicitly narrower than preferred generic concept M0045998. Thus the heading is a broader anchor, not exact L-specific identity. PubMed 2870828 confirms use of the L-named substrate. Scope: The metatraits_gtdb normalized label explicitly specifies L and its blank raw label is preserved. An exact mesh:C004813 replacement would discard the stereochemical scope despite the flattened OLS synonym. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-167 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[167] case_id=KG_CASE:7948bf1ec77fe9f7edc45136563351f4d43f551dbb2451a564a1de32bc9cabde | partial | The source is 0.5 mL of 0.1% w/v sodium resazurin and carries salt CAS 62758-13-8/mass 251.17. The current CHEBI:8806 owner denotes neutral resazurin (CAS 550-82-3), so both sodium salt and prepared-stock scope are lost by exact reuse. Scope: The source attribute is essential: this is a stock addition rather than a weighed free-acid ingredient. No synonym on Resazurin.yaml can by itself approve the different supplied entity. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-168 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[168] case_id=KG_CASE:8130043b63c67f0e4b6ab8c93d89c601ec5b2bd6e53c7ef29acc636315297af5 | partial | CAS 68-19-9 and the source chemical fields identify cyanocobalamin, CHEBI:17439. CHEBI:176843 vitamin B12 denotes the broader vitamin class and does not authorize moving this precise chemical into a generic-vitamer identity. Scope: The Cyanocobalamine spelling on source 847 is supported for the Cyanocobalamin owner. The Vitamin_B12 overlap needs alias-scope reconciliation, not merging every cobalamin form. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-169 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[169] case_id=KG_CASE:81beda652081417213eba4c3d21b7e273575263949bd6bf1647eeeb0e0e76bfa | partial | MediaDive gives trisodium-NTA CAS 5064-31-3 and a 3Na formula, but DSMZ 1560 names only Na-Nitrilotriacetat without sodium stoichiometry or hydrate state. Automatically supplied cross-references do not independently establish which sodium salt was ordered. Scope: The abbreviated trace-stock label is not equivalent to the explicitly trisodium monohydrate case 1930; the existing unmapped owner correctly preserves that unresolved specificity. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-170 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[170] case_id=KG_CASE:87a3023cb2b6523988122d33d722774edb88942f02c97e21dd816a7954a0e850 | partial | The source specifies CMRL 1066, GIBCO 042-1545, glutamine-containing 10x formulation and 100 mL addition. It is a commercial multi-component medium, not a molecule or every product carrying the CMRL 1066 name. Scope: The frozen source attributes supply concentration and catalogue context; aliases naming other catalogues on the owner do not prove identical formulation or packaging. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-171 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[171] case_id=KG_CASE:8c75bfd344f2684dbebc66b342e002ae275248698f46f09945b1580400579684 | partial | ATCC 25646 describes Streptomyces padanus as producing Etabetacin with antibacterial/antitumour activity. This confirms a named biological product, but not its chemical structure or exact registry identity. The exact OLS name query returned no hit. Scope: The metatraits source has blank raw label and a normalized etabetacin name; neither organism production nor activity identifies a unique structure or supplied preparation for this case. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-172 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[172] case_id=KG_CASE:8e4d3cf9aef1f84007b584b506027e319f8285647083af699d0cbdecc1de4a62 | partial | The source CAS 532-32-1 and sodium-benzoate name agree with CHEBI:113455 and the existing Na-benzoate owner. Benzoic acid is a separate supplied form. Scope: Sodiumbenzoate is a spacing variant in ingredient 1562; the chemical identity evidence does not independently approve all inherited alias/role payload on the owner. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-173 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[173] case_id=KG_CASE:8f368d39ec935e5ff4951158e77e38c8bb2a34484ce5ae79a0eaf1c475a4b3a0 | partial | Sigma T0647 supplies TAPS sodium salt CAS 91000-53-2, with sodium-containing formula and structure. CHEBI:191055 is the free acid, CAS 29915-38-6, and serves only as a broader parent. The current form-specific CAS identity is supported. Scope: Source 1083 explicitly says sodium salt and agrees with the Sigma product; bare TAPS aliases or product text mentioning other cations cannot erase that sodium-specific scope. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-174 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[174] case_id=KG_CASE:9ab36ad4b322d429ea1ed8d1f9a678f746bdb6d938737f0537bb177e19061565 | partial | Native NLM resolves the apparent OLS synonym match: the L-alanine-4-nitroanilide concept is narrower than the generic alanine-4-nitroanilide heading mesh:C004813. PubMed names the L substrate, but does not make the generic heading an exact stereo-specific identifier. Scope: This metatraits case is separate from metatraits_gtdb despite the same normalized label. Blank raw source text remains blank; no racemic or unqualified substrate is substituted. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-175 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[175] case_id=KG_CASE:a6b19d14188dc7b9dfec1be11bc0fa0847f929b724b529324189d2f897bb9bf0 | partial | DSMZ 672 says half-strength nutrient broth or agar, Difco 0003 or Difco 0001. It identifies a commercial medium option and dilution context, but does not supply a complete formulation or justify merging broth and agar versions. Scope: The raw 2132 catalogue token is a product reference rather than a chemical name; alternatives in the recipe cannot be collapsed into a single pure-substance identity. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-176 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[176] case_id=KG_CASE:ac6686c0d61be7f652dcf0c2a495b463e1adf24fee613329fd02707bd19d759d | partial | CAS 10034-99-8 and the seven-water solute label agree with CHEBI:31795. However the source row is 10 mL of a 7.5 g/L stock; exact reuse of the pure magnesium sulfate heptahydrate owner would erase preparation and concentration. Scope: Parentheses/spacing normalization is harmless for solute identification, but the raw attribute and volume make this particular occurrence a prepared solution. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-177 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[177] case_id=KG_CASE:ae8ae53404df18ce150c7bb93e25c7bf473b5b2bdbef690747ad9fa78b44ece7 | partial | The source label explicitly says L-cysteine HCl, but MediaDive attaches racemic-hydrochloride CAS 10318-18-0 and QSY9 CHEBI:52891. The label suggests CHEBI:91247 but the contradictory independent fields remain unresolved. Scope: This source 1157 cannot be approved through the current L-specific owner simply because one field matches; unrelated dye cross-reference and water-state ambiguity must be source-corrected. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-178 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[178] case_id=KG_CASE:b5fe6f2f30ffe4512e90b14ef0b7f557d89f28865fb4bc9dffae123dd178f277 | partial | JCM 1081/1082 refer to JCM 1079, whose basal NaCl medium contains NaCl, K2HPO4, NH4Cl and HEPES, with additional separately prepared supplements. This establishes a source recipe, not sodium chloride identity. Scope: The Basal mineral NaCl medium row must preserve the basal-versus-supplement boundary; treating the complete supplemented growth medium as the stock would change its composition. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-180 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[180] case_id=KG_CASE:c26a75f93ba943b7c3d2b086d2f8854de0b53cd6bf718cb2f82686da5ef8bffb | partial | JCM 758 explicitly prints trisodium citrate monohydrate. The current mesh:C514290 grounding does not independently establish that specific water state, and the source supplies no form-specific CAS. It is not safe to replace the label with common dihydrate. Scope: This case is ingredient 1888 with one water, separate from the trihydrate case 1997 and citrate acid/salt classes. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-181 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[181] case_id=KG_CASE:c35f85e70ce97bd55f770143509729bfb301a1768aa70f4c5fe37f12fc848e9b | partial | The source explicitly names Oxoid CM0957 at 35.4 g. The manufacturer specification provides the matching 15-component dehydrated anaerobe basal broth formulation and total mass, supporting an exact commercial product scope. Scope: The evidence resolves this catalogue-specific product as a mixture, not a single chemical. It does not establish that every generic Fastidious Anaerobe Basal Broth label is the same product/version. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
| case-182 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[182] case_id=KG_CASE:dcd55a5ebcd552423dbd4675ae8236528f505692b77b04feba3feed9f075edf1 | partial | DSMZ 1600 uses one pack of L-15 medium powder in a separately supplemented 2x preparation. This is a commercial cell-culture-medium formulation and the stock preparation includes other ingredients; neither the pack size nor catalogue variant is specified in this row. Scope: Source 2153 must retain powder/package and recipe context; generic L-15 names alone do not distinguish variants or certify the final supplemented mixture. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
