| case-184 | reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/root-native-input-decisions.json; decisions[184] case_id=KG_CASE:e3f11fbd29d1d0f932986cc7179ec7190be4345af8b35da405a39816812a32fb | partial | Source CAS 137-08-6 identifies calcium D-pantothenate, CHEBI:31345. Four vanillylamide/Zostrix aliases on its current owner instead occur on CHEBI:3374 capsaicin, a chemically different substance; they are demonstrably foreign identity labels. Scope: The proposal preserves the source spelling Calcium panthothenate and marks only those four capsaicin labels REJECTED_LABEL. It does not approve other DL/stereo aliases, roles or the complete published payload. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization. |
