- evidence_id: authority-1355
  kind: authority
  reference: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?iri=http%3A%2F%2Fpurl.obolibrary.org%2Fobo%2FCHEBI_52891
  locator: Term label, definition, synonym scope and chemistry annotations; exact
    local capture captures/c-chebi-52891.json
  accessed_at: '2026-11-08T05:08:05.640785Z'
  support: refutes
  summary: Cysteine-HCl carries neither L nor D in its source label. MediaDive links
    CAS 10318-18-0 and CHEBI:52891; the latter is QSY9 succinimidyl ester rather than
    cysteine. The existing L-cysteine hydrochloride owner cannot supply missing stereochemistry.;
    JCM 680 names an L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate solution but gives no concentration
    for the 10 mL addition. The local stock identity therefore remains separate from
    the pure solute. CHEBI:52891 and the Thermo QSY9 product show that its QSY9 synonym
    is a different dye and must remain non-resolving provenance.; The source label
    explicitly says L-cysteine HCl, but MediaDive attaches racemic-hydrochloride CAS
    10318-18-0 and QSY9 CHEBI:52891. The label suggests CHEBI:91247 but the contradictory
    independent fields remain unresolved.
  snapshot_sha256: 2b32913d5ab8bbc296bb5fbdc0340190cf6212655819134b99b0581ed06c0b70
