  - case-168
  details: 'Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12): Both source occurrences explicitly say Cyanocobalamin,
    with VitaminB12 as a parenthetical gloss. CCAP stock4 and NBRC1550 support this
    named vitamer; the frozen CHEBI176843 class on one occurrence is broader than
    the explicit compound. CHEBI17439 is the matching cyanocobalamin identity. Add
    only this fully qualified alias, not generic VitaminB12. Remaining requirement:
    None


    Cyanocobalamine (vitamin B12): DSMZ958 and Togo M2300 explicitly name cyanocobalamine
    with vitamin B12 parenthetical. The cyano-qualified substance is CHEBI17439; the
    broader vitamin-B12 class CHEBI176843 does not replace that specificity. Remaining
    requirement: None


    Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin): The complete frozen UTEX DAS cocktail occurrence explicitly
    names Sigma V6629 in its ingredient evidence. The original UTEX recipe repeats
    that catalog, and the official supplier identifies V6629 as cyanocobalamin, CAS68-19-9.
    Therefore this occurrence supports cyanocobalamin rather than merely the unspecified
    vitaminB12 class. The product specification, not the5.9µM quantity or generic
    word cobalamin, establishes the vitamer. Remaining requirement: Apply only the
    source-bound UTEX DAS occurrence correction to CHEBI:17439; no global Vitamin
    B12 (Cobalamin) alias is proposed. Preserve the original label and source sterilization
    instructions.


    Cyanocobalamin (B12): The P5 RS NM component explicitly names Cyanocobalamin (B12),
    so its frozen vitamin-B12 class pointer is broader than the stated vitamer. The
    nested stock rate 1 g/L describes the cyanocobalamin solute, not the identity
    or full carrier formulation of the stock. Remaining requirement: None


    mediadive.ingredient:847: CAS 68-19-9 and the source chemical fields identify
    cyanocobalamin, CHEBI:17439. CHEBI:176843 vitamin B12 denotes the broader vitamin
    class and does not authorize moving this precise chemical into a generic-vitamer
    identity. Remaining requirement: Reconcile the competing vitamin-class alias and
    inherited owner-payload holds before source consumption.'
