- assessment_id: owner-assessment-013
  area: identity
  topic: Assigned source-label, supplied-form and synonym comparison
  outcome: supported
  summary: Compared Ground beef (FOODON:00001282) to 4 assigned source cases. No owner-byte
    change is proposed by these cases. Support is limited to the explicit case relation
    or contrast; no complete owner approval.
  target_ids:
  - data/ingredients/mapped/Ground_Beef.yaml
  evidence_ids:
  - owner-013
  - campaign-evidence
  - case-002
  - case-050
  - case-100
  - case-131
  details: 'Ground beef (fat-free): The three chopped-meat source recipes use fat-free
    ground beef as a heterogeneous animal tissue preparation. They are neither beef
    extract nor a single purified nutrient. The source-specific removal of fat and
    subsequent meat processing must remain attached to each recipe; no exact alias
    to a generic beef ingredient is supported. Remaining requirement: Compare each
    original ATCC chopped-meat preparation, including defatting/cooking and any permitted
    tissue substitutions, before asserting one reusable supplied-material owner.


    Ground beef (fat free): The eighteen occurrences retain fat-free ground beef,
    but come from DSMZ/ATCC/JCM chopped-meat formulations and normalized KOMODO variants.
    The primary recipes include meat processing and possible tissue substitutions.
    These heterogeneous tissue preparations must not collapse to beef extract or to
    one exact processed product from spelling alone. Remaining requirement: Compare
    the original meat preparation and any allowed substitution per occurrence before
    assigning a single supplied-material identity; retain the three KOMODO-derived
    concentration values independently.


    Ground beef (free of fat): ATCC593/735-derived occurrences explicitly require
    ground beef free of fat; preparation then produces cooked meat medium. The generic
    ground-beef term does not encode fat removal or the extracted/cooked product.
    Raw beef input, filtrate and complete broth remain separate. Remaining requirement:
    Retain fat-removal preparation in source/product metadata; reconcile the intended
    source-qualified material scope with the generic Ground_Beef owner before adding
    a resolving alias.


    Ground Beef (fat-free): M2713/M2721 retain Ground Beef (fat-free) as raw material
    for chopped-meat carbohydrate formulations. Fat removal, subsequent cooking and
    broth assembly must not be discarded or equated with generic ground beef product
    scope. Remaining requirement: Reconcile source-specific fat-free meat preparation
    and the generic beef owner; do not turn a preparation-qualified input into a blanket
    synonym for every ground-beef product.'
  dimensions:
