    L--Cysteine・H2O・HCl: JCM552 explicitly specifies L-cysteine·H2O·HCl; JCM553 and627
    inherit that recipe with named changes that do not alter this component. The six
    frozen spellings retain L configuration, hydrochloride and one water. CHEBI91248
    independently describes that exact form, so a typed raw alias on the active hydrate
    owner is justified. Remaining requirement: None


    Cysteine-hydrochloride: TOGO M3149 confirms the unspecific cysteine-hydrochloride
    label but no stereochemistry or hydrate. Live issue905 documents that similarly
    unspecific MediaDive metadata conflicts among DL anhydrous and L hydrate identifiers.
    The frozen obsolete MediaIngredientMech numeric reference is not identity authority.
    Remaining requirement: Obtain original DSM135 formulation or supplier/CAS establishing
    stereochemistry and water content; do not inherit either CHEBI91247 or91248 from
    an unspecific alias.


    L-Cysteine . HCl . H2O: TOGO M2575 retains explicit L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate
    in its cysteine/sulfide reducing solution. Membership inside a stock does not
    make this component the whole stock. The source string preserves L configuration
    and one water and matches CHEBI91248, supporting a raw-form alias only. Remaining
    requirement: None


    Cysteine HCl x H2O: TOGO M2598 confirms Cysteine HCl xH2O but the name and available
    recipe text do not establish L versus DL. CHEBI91248 is L specific. A one-water
    suffix resolves hydration but cannot resolve stereochemistry. Remaining requirement:
    Obtain supplier/CAS or explicit stereochemical wording for the cysteine hydrochloride
    monohydrate in ATCC Methanogenium medium.


    mediadive.ingredient:1114: Ingredient 1114 names cysteine hydrochloride without
