    records already contain a content-bound scientific hold: the 1992 source prints
    NaMoO4.2H2O, while a later formulation has Na2MoO4.2H2O. Their source notes explicitly
    prohibit repairing the sodium count or borrowing the later article. A failed new
    paper retrieval does not weaken that hold. Remaining requirement: Resolve the
    printed 1992 one-sodium formula through an erratum or original authors’ material
    specification; retain source mass and unverified database molarity separately.


    Na2MoO3·2H2O: NBRC302 and305 both retain Na2MoO3·2H2O, rather than the Na2MoO4·2H2O
    formula of CHEBI75213. The four frozen occurrences inherit this source-level formula
    conflict and milligram-to-gram flattening. Oxygen count cannot be silently repaired
    as lexical normalization. Remaining requirement: An NBRC correction, original
    recipe or supplier/CAS must establish whether the MoO3 label denotes molybdate
    or another compound; preserve the exact O3 source spelling meanwhile.


    Na2MoO4·4H2O: NBRC1333 explicitly prints Na2MoO4·4H2O in a 1000x stock. The formula
    names four waters, not the existing dihydrate CHEBI75213. Its recipe amount is
    0.1 g in 100 ml, not necessarily the frozen final-medium concentration. Preserve
    the four-water claim until the actual reagent is established. Remaining requirement:
    Obtain the original NBRC1333 molybdate reagent specification/CAS or an erratum
    resolving the tetrahydrate; do not reuse the dihydrate by convention.


    mediadive.ingredient:1678: The ingredient 1678 API points to JCM 196. The primary
    JCM 196 recipe states Na2MoO4·2H2O at the corresponding 3 microgram trace-element
    row, independently resolving this source label Na2MoO7 x 2 H2O as a transcription
    error for sodium molybdate dihydrate. CHEBI:75213 has that exact form. Remaining
    requirement: A source-bound override/correction referencing JCM 196 is needed
    for consumption; existing held owner aliases require separate review.


    mediadive.ingredient:1416: DSMZ 1560 itself prints Na2MoO7O4 x 2 H2O in the mineral
    stock, so the malformed source formula has not been independently corrected. A
    separate trace-stock row uses Na2MoO4; that does not prove both rows name the
    same supplied form. Remaining requirement: Obtain a corrected DSMZ 1560 formulation
    or product/CAS certificate for the mineral-stock row before routing ingredient
    1416 to dihydrate CHEBI:75213.


    mediadive.ingredient:1503: The explicit dihydrate label and CAS 10102-40-6 match
    CHEBI:75213 sodium molybdate dihydrate. The extra space after Na2 is only typography
    in this source case. Remaining requirement: Keep source-specific and owner-payload
    holds until each affected alias/context is reviewed.


    mediadive.ingredient:9: The exact Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O wording and CAS 10102-40-6 agree
    with CHEBI:75213. This is the dihydrate, not the anhydrous CHEBI:75215 record
    or the unresolved one-water source. Remaining requirement: Complete native owner
    payload review and source-bound hold reconciliation before downstream consumption.'
  dimensions:
  - name: claim_scope
    value: source identity/form/alias only
    definition: No roles, unrelated source identities, full chemical properties or
      content-bound publication support approved.
