  - case-109
  details: 'Sodium citrate・2H2O: JCM704 and the frozen JCM833 lineage name sodium
    citrate dihydrate. CHEBI32142 uses that same chemical name for trisodium citrate
    dihydrate. The two-water qualification is explicit and retained; add the exact
    punctuation spelling to the active Na3-citrate dihydrate owner, never to anhydrous
    citrate. This is a documented conventional substance name: independent Sigma W302600
    and Thermo S279 specifications explicitly equate sodium citrate dihydrate with
    trisodium citrate dihydrate, CAS6132-04-3, matching CHEBI32142. This nomenclature
    evidence supports the name-to-substance interpretation only; it does not assert
    that JCM bought either supplier product. Bare sodium NTA/malate lacks an equivalently
    specific hydrate-qualified naming witness in these cases. Remaining requirement:
    None


    Sodium citrate·2H2O: JCM1331 titanium-citrate stock and JCM1492 iron stock explicitly
    use sodium citrate·2H2O. The solid input is sodium citrate dihydrate CHEBI32142,
    not the resulting titanium/iron solution. Add the exact spelling only; source
    amount/final-volume discrepancies belong to recipe correction, not identity. This
    is a documented conventional substance name: independent Sigma W302600 and Thermo
    S279 specifications explicitly equate sodium citrate dihydrate with trisodium
    citrate dihydrate, CAS6132-04-3, matching CHEBI32142. This nomenclature evidence
    supports the name-to-substance interpretation only; it does not assert that JCM
    bought either supplier product. Bare sodium NTA/malate lacks an equivalently specific
    hydrate-qualified naming witness in these cases. Remaining requirement: None


    Sodium citrate tribasic dihydrate: M3175 explicitly names sodium citrate tribasic
    dihydrate. Tribasic fixes three sodium ions and dihydrate fixes two waters, exactly
    CHEBI32142; no mono/disodium citrate or trihydrate alias is justified. Remaining
    requirement: None'
